uested subjunctive uses base **translate**, without third-person -s.","keywords":["mandative-base"],"skill":"mandative-base","contextKey":"unreal-subjunctive-4","fingerprint":"4b00639ab34ec7c3b45b99ba73528dc44055623b947ad67a7bb99becbc98ac7b","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-unreal"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["The clause expresses a **recommendation**, and the requested form is the **subjunctive**.","The requested subjunctive uses base **translate**, without third-person -s.","Choose **translate**. Read the complete sentence again and check both its form and its intended meaning."],"choiceReasons":{"A":"The requested subjunctive uses base **translate**, without third-person -s.","B":"This is ordinary indicative agreement, not the explicitly requested subjunctive form.","C":"The subjunctive here uses a base form, not past tense.","D":"A finite that-clause in this pattern does not use a to-infinitive."}}},{"id":"57c4287d-bc37-5cca-adf5-8e41322def5b","topicSlug":"unreal-subjunctive","level":"C1","prompt":"Use a negative mandative subjunctive: “They insist that she ____ the travel leaflet without permission.”","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"not to translate"},{"id":"B","text":"not translate"},{"id":"C","text":"does not translate"},{"id":"D","text":"not translates"}],"answerId":"B","hint":"A mandative negative places **not directly before the base verb**.","explanation":"The negative subjunctive is **not + base translate**, without does.","keywords":["negative-subjunctive"],"skill":"negative-subjunctive","contextKey":"unreal-subjunctive-4","fingerprint":"4357231ed489b64fa644e2ff9b9598e3971ccf599a7a2a50d0d042afd4cb1331","source":"seed","provenance":{"kind":"original-guidance-aligned","referenceIds":["bc-unreal"],"version":"core-2026-09-v3","reviewStatus":"automated-checked; educator-review-pending"},"teaching":{"steps":["A mandative negative